[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 395,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 228,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58405,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 228,
        "headingText": "<p>Acral fibromyxoma is a benign fibroblastic neoplasm with a marked predilection for the subungual and periungual aspects of the digits and potential for local recurrence.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-30T11:16:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 396,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 229,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58406,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 229,
        "headingText": "<p>8811/0 Acral fibromyxoma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-31T09:25:34"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 397,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 230,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58407,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 230,
        "headingText": "<p>EE6Y &amp; XH5XQ3 Other specified fibromatous disorders of skin and soft tissue &amp; Fibromyxoma</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-01-23T16:18:48"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 398,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 231,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58408,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 231,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> superficial acral fibromyxoma; digital fibromyxoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> cellular digital fibroma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 399,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 232,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58409,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 232,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 400,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 233,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58410,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 233,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>There is a strong predilection for the periungual and subungual aspects of the fingers and toes {28045748; 22367301; 18764846; 18537858; 11486169}. Other areas of the hands and feet, ankles, wrists, lower legs, and thighs may rarely be affected {22367301; 27825811}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 401,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 234,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58411,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 234,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxomas present as slowly enlarging and frequently painful solitary tumours, typically measuring 1&ndash;2&nbsp;cm {28045748; 22367301; 18764846; 18537858}. The tumours may cause nail deformity, and erosive or lytic lesions of the underlying bone may be detected radiographically {22367301}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 402,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 235,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58412,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 235,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A wide age range is affected, but most tumours present in middle-aged adults, with a median age of about 50&nbsp;years. Males are more frequently affected than females {11486169; 22367301}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 403,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 236,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58413,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 236,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 404,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 237,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58414,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 237,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>RB1</em> deletions have been reported {27825811}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 411,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 244,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58415,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 244,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>On macroscopic examination, the tumours appear dome-shaped, polypoid, or verrucoid, with soft to firm consistency, an often lobulated aspect, and poorly defined borders.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 405,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 238,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58416,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 238,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxomas present in dermis and subcutis as lobulated tumours, occasionally with a polypoid growth and surrounding epidermal collarette formation. The majority of tumours show an infiltrative growth pattern, with rare invasion of underlying bone. The tumours are composed of bland-appearing spindled or stellate cells arranged loosely in a variably myxoid or collagenous stroma. Scattered multinucleated cells may be admixed. A vaguely storiform or fascicular growth pattern may be seen, and a proliferation of small vascular channels is present in the myxoid areas. Cartilaginous or osseous metaplasia is rarely observed. Nuclear pleomorphism and tumour necrosis are absent, and mitoses are rare. By immunohistochemistry, the tumour cells express CD34 and occasionally EMA and SMA. There is loss of RB1 expression in the majority of tumours {27825811}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 406,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 239,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58417,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 239,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 407,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 240,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58418,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 240,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours show deletion of the <em>RB1</em> gene {27825811}, but this is not required.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 410,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 243,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58419,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 243,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> acral, usually periungual location; dermal-based tumour with infiltration of subcutis; lobulated architecture with vaguely storiform or fascicular growth; bland spindle cells in a variably myxoid or collagenous matrix.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> CD34 positivity and frequent loss of RB1 expression by immunohistochemistry.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 408,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 241,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58420,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 241,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 409,
    "bookid": 33,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 242,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 58421,
        "bookId": 33,
        "chapterId": 109,
        "headingId": 242,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Acral fibromyxomas recur locally in as many as 22% of cases. Local recurrences are non-destructive and can be cured by re-excision. Metastases have not been reported {11486169; 22367301}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-12-11T11:21:51"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]